  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 25 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nPrivate. Secure. Beautifully renovated. \r\n\r\nTucked away down a private driveway, this beautifully renovated three-bedroom home delivers exceptional privacy, contemporary elegance and effortless coastal living.\r\n\r\nJust a short stroll from Madills Farm, Tamaki Drive, the waterfront and St Heliers village, the location is outstanding.\r\n\r\nShowcasing quality finishes throughout, the home features beautiful timber flooring, plantation shutters, skylights and a stunning entertainer's kitchen with premium Bosch appliances, bespoke cabinetry and Häfele fittings.\r\n\r\nLight-filled living spaces flow through bifold doors to a sunny, north-facing courtyard, perfect for entertaining. Two separate living areas and two private balconies offer space to relax and unwind.\r\n\r\n\r\nProperty Highlights\r\n\r\n• 3 generous bedrooms and 2 beautifully renovated bathrooms\r\n\r\n• Stunning kitchen with premium Bosch appliances\r\n\r\n• Two separate living areas and two private balconies\r\n\r\n• Sunny, north-facing entertaining courtyard\r\n\r\n• Timber flooring, skylights and plantation shutters\r\n\r\n• Double internal-access garage plus 3 off-street parks\r\n\r\n• Exceptional privacy in a secure setting\r\n\r\n• Walk to Madills Farm, the waterfront and St Heliers village\r\n\r\n• Zoned for Kohimarama School and Glendowie College\r\n\r\n\r\nBeautifully renovated. Wonderfully private. Perfectly positioned.\r\n\r\nAuction Wednesday 25 November - Don't Miss Your Opportunity!\r\n\r\nWith auction day fast approaching, now is the time to act. Contact us today to arrange your private viewing.\r\n\r\nAll agent conjunctionals are welcome and encouraged.",
